ns4:enhancedDescription a rdf:Property ;
    rdfs:label "enhanced description"@en ;
    ns4:markdownDescription "The property can be used in several scenarios the simplest being to refer to an RDF document that provides additional context about a resource. This alone adds little more than rdfs:seeAlso.\\n\\nHowever it is expected that typically a user agent may be issued with an authentication challenge (e.g. at the HTTP protocol level) when attempting to access the document. This would support delivery of \"premium\" views of a resource as Linked Data. Using this property a user agent could distinguish those documents from others that are simply referred to with an rdfs:seeAlso."@en ;
    ns1:plural "enhanced descriptions"@en ;
    ns3:etag "09a37218-ac62-494c-9b02-27aee3f6e129" ;
    rdfs:comment "This property is to be used to relate a resource to an \"enhanced description\". An enhanced description is one that provides additional, richer detail about a resource than may typically be obtained by a simple de-reference of the resource's URI."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy onto: ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf rdfs:seeAlso ;
    ns2:term_status "unstable" ;
    ns2:userdocs ns4:enhancedDescription.html .

